/*
We have a rectangle [0,w] x [0,h].
There are n almonds at given points.
There are m allowed cut lines, each connecting a point on left edge (0, a)
to a point on right edge (w, b). So each cut is a segment y(x)=a+(b-a)x/w.

A single cut divides the chocolate into two connected pieces, so Shi-ta can
always take one side and Be-ko the other. Be-ko needs area >= S and wants to
minimize almonds on her side.

Thus for every allowed line, consider both half-planes inside the rectangle:
- below the line
- above the line
Their areas are A and w*h-A. If one is >= S, it is a feasible Be-ko piece.
Count almonds strictly on that side? Points on the cut belong to both boundary.
For such partition, almonds on boundary remain with either piece? Standard
geometry partition problems usually count points on/in the chosen piece, and
boundary belongs to both closures. But since cut passes through chocolate,
almonds on the cut cannot be split. The intended handling is that almonds on
the line belong to neither side choice ambiguity? To avoid ambiguity, we use:
below side includes points with y < line, above side includes y > line, and
points on line are excluded from both counts. This matches minimizing almonds
on one side when cut passes through almonds: those almonds are cut and thus not
on Be-ko's piece. This is the usual interpretation for such problems.

Area below line within the rectangle:
integral_0^w y(x) dx = w*(a+b)/2.
But line can go outside [0,h]; however endpoints are on left/right edges, so
a,b are in [0,h], hence whole segment stays inside rectangle. Good.

So:
A_below = w*(a+b)/2
A_above = w*h - A_below

For each almond (x,y), compare with line:
y ? a + (b-a)x/w
Multiply by w:
y*w ? a*w + (b-a)*x

Count below/above.

Take minimum feasible count.

Input format is not explicitly given in statement excerpt, so we assume the
common format:
w h
n
x1 y1
...
xn yn
m
a1 b1
...
am bm
S

To be safer, implement token-based parser and read all numbers:
Need at least 5 values. We'll parse in that order.

All coordinates and S may be integers; use long for exact arithmetic.
*/

public class Main {
    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        long nextLong() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
            } while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);
            long sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }
            long val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);

        long w, h;
        try {
            w = fs.nextLong();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return;
        }
        h = fs.nextLong();

        int n = (int) fs.nextLong();
        long[] xs = new long[n];
        long[] ys = new long[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            xs[i] = fs.nextLong();
            ys[i] = fs.nextLong();
        }

        int m = (int) fs.nextLong();
        long[] a = new long[m];
        long[] b = new long[m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            a[i] = fs.nextLong();
            b[i] = fs.nextLong();
        }

        long S = fs.nextLong();

        long totalArea2 = 2L * w * h; // doubled area
        long need2 = 2L * S;

        int ans = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            long belowArea2 = w * (a[i] + b[i]); // doubled area below
            long aboveArea2 = totalArea2 - belowArea2;

            int belowCnt = 0, aboveCnt = 0;
            long aw = a[i] * w;
            long diff = b[i] - a[i];

            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                long lhs = ys[j] * w;
                long rhs = aw + diff * xs[j];
                if (lhs < rhs) belowCnt++;
                else if (lhs > rhs) aboveCnt++;
            }

            if (belowArea2 >= need2) ans = Math.min(ans, belowCnt);
            if (aboveArea2 >= need2) ans = Math.min(ans, aboveCnt);
        }

        if (ans == Integer.MAX_VALUE) ans = -1;
        System.out.println(ans);
    }
